---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const structuredData = {
	"@context": "https://schema.org",
	"@type": "SoftwareApplication",
	name: "Get Good Grades",
	applicationCategory: "Desktop flashcard application",
	operatingSystem: "Cross-platform (Electron)",
	description:
		"A desktop flashcard application built with Electron, React, TypeScript, and YAML, that reads user-controlled .yaml deck files directly from the local file system instead of a centralized service.",
	author: {
		"@type": "Person",
		name: "Atishaya Maharjan",
		url: "https://atishaya7777.github.io",
	},
};
---

<Layout
	title="Get Good Grades — Atishaya Maharjan"
	description="Get Good Grades: a desktop flashcard app built with Electron, React, TypeScript, and YAML that reads user-controlled flashcard decks from the local file system. Winner, 'Most Chaotic Evil Hack,' .devHacks 2026."
	type="article"
	structuredData={structuredData}
>
	<article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6">

		<header class="pt-20 pb-10 text-center">
			<p class="text-xs tracking-[0.25em] uppercase text-ink-400 dark:text-ink-300 mb-6">
				Project&nbsp;Note
			</p>
			<h1 class="font-display font-medium text-4xl sm:text-5xl text-ink-900 dark:text-ink-100 leading-tight mb-4">
				Get Good Grades
			</h1>
			<p class="text-base text-ink-500 dark:text-ink-300 max-w-xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
				A desktop flashcard app that keeps your decks as plain YAML files instead of a database you don't control.
			</p>
		</header>

		<section class="pb-10">
			<dl class="grid grid-cols-[110px_1fr] gap-x-6 gap-y-2 text-sm max-w-xl mx-auto">
				<dt class="text-ink-400 dark:text-ink-300 uppercase text-xs tracking-[0.1em] pt-0.5">Type</dt>
				<dd class="text-ink-700 dark:text-ink-200">Personal / hackathon project</dd>

				<dt class="text-ink-400 dark:text-ink-300 uppercase text-xs tracking-[0.1em] pt-0.5">Role</dt>
				<dd class="text-ink-700 dark:text-ink-200">Sole designer and developer</dd>

				<dt class="text-ink-400 dark:text-ink-300 uppercase text-xs tracking-[0.1em] pt-0.5">Stack</dt>
				<dd class="text-ink-700 dark:text-ink-200">Electron · React · TypeScript · YAML</dd>

				<dt class="text-ink-400 dark:text-ink-300 uppercase text-xs tracking-[0.1em] pt-0.5">Event</dt>
				<dd class="text-ink-700 dark:text-ink-200">.devHacks 2026 — "Most Chaotic Evil Hack"</dd>

				<dt class="text-ink-400 dark:text-ink-300 uppercase text-xs tracking-[0.1em] pt-0.5">Source</dt>
				<dd class="text-ink-700 dark:text-ink-200">Not currently public</dd>
			</dl>
		</section>

		<hr class="border-t-4 border-double border-ink-900 dark:border-ink-100" />

		<section class="py-12">
			<h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-ink-900 dark:text-ink-100 mb-6">
				<span class="text-ink-400 dark:text-ink-300 mr-2">1.</span>The Idea
			</h2>
			<div class="space-y-4 text-[15px] leading-[1.8]">
				<p>
					Most flashcard apps lock your decks inside a proprietary database or a cloud account. Get Good
					Grades instead reads flashcard decks directly from user-controlled <code>.yaml</code> files on the
					local file system — the content and the viewer are kept separate, so a deck is just a plain-text
					file you can create, edit, organize, and share however you like, without depending on the app's own
					storage.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<hr class="border-rule dark:border-rule-dark" />

		<section class="py-12">
			<h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-ink-900 dark:text-ink-100 mb-6">
				<span class="text-ink-400 dark:text-ink-300 mr-2">2.</span>The Build
			</h2>
			<div class="space-y-4 text-[15px] leading-[1.8]">
				<p>
					I designed and built the application as an Electron desktop app with a React and TypeScript
					frontend. The core design decision was to keep flashcard content as YAML rather than in a
					database, so decks stay portable, human-readable, and shareable as plain text — no proprietary
					format, no account required.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<hr class="border-rule dark:border-rule-dark" />

		<section class="py-12">
			<h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-ink-900 dark:text-ink-100 mb-6">
				<span class="text-ink-400 dark:text-ink-300 mr-2">3.</span>Recognition
			</h2>
			<div class="space-y-4 text-[15px] leading-[1.8]">
				<p>
					I presented Get Good Grades at <strong class="font-semibold text-ink-900 dark:text-ink-100">.devHacks 2026</strong>,
					where it received the "Most Chaotic Evil Hack" award.
				</p>
			</div>
			{/*
				TODO (Atishaya): this page still needs the screenshots, a short demo (link or GIF), and
				an example of the YAML deck format you mentioned. Send those and I'll add a figure
				gallery here, matching the EkNepal page's pattern. I deliberately didn't invent a YAML
				schema or demo link since I haven't seen either.
			*/}
		</section>

	</article>
</Layout>
